# ── Test-only ports and paths ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ★ This file holds **every** convention of the test environment; the
#   development environment never reads it.
#   Both sides (Go and Vite) take their values from here, so that ports do not
#   end up scattered across the Makefile, playwright.config.ts and each smoke
#   script — changing a port would mean touching five files, and missing one
#   means "the test mysteriously hit the development server".
#
# ★ The ports are **completely separate** from development, for these reasons:
#   1. Running tests while vite (5173) and openheron (8080) are up should not
#      make them compete;
#   2. More importantly, **state**: openheron keeps its sessions under the
#      config root's state/ directory, and a test writing there pollutes the
#      real session history;
#   3. A taken port silently changes what is being tested — when the
#      development server is reused, `OPENHERON_API_TARGET` is never injected,
#      so the test is "all green" while talking to the real backend
#      (this trap was hit once; see the comment in web/playwright.config.ts).
#
# Usage: on the bash side `set -a; . ./.env.test; set +a`; on the Vite side it
# is read by loadEnv(mode, repoRoot, "OPENHERON_") (see web/vite.config.ts).

# ── Backend (the real openheron, used by the smoke and protocol tests) ──────
OPENHERON_TEST_BACKEND_PORT=18099
OPENHERON_TEST_BACKEND_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:18099

# The isolated config and data root. Relative paths are resolved against the
# repository root at startup.
# Under OPENHERON_TEST_ROOT the script creates project/.openheron/ (the
# project-level configuration) and state/ (the sessions).
OPENHERON_TEST_ROOT=.openheron-test

# ── Backend (the fake backend, used by E2E; keeps the UI tests deterministic) ─
OPENHERON_TEST_FAKE_PORT=18180

# ── Frontend (Vite) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
OPENHERON_TEST_FRONTEND_PORT=15173
OPENHERON_TEST_FRONTEND_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:15173
